L("the-value-of-work","economic-and-non-economic-activities","Economic and non-economic activities","Meena's mother goes to an office while her grandmother cooks and cares for children at home.\n\"Both are work,\" said Meena.",
 ["Economic activities are work done to earn money, such as farming, teaching, driving and selling. Non-economic activities are done out of love or duty without pay, like cooking for the family or helping neighbours.","Non-economic work is just as important because it supports families and communities.","Community participation, such as cleaning the street together, shows the value of work for everyone."],
 ["economic activity","non-economic activity","volunteer"],("Is cooking at home economic or non-economic?",[("It is not done for pay.","Pay."),("It is for the family.","Family."),("It is non-economic work.","Answer.")]),
 ("only work that earns money is important.",["Non-economic work matters too.","It supports families."],["Narrow."]),
 ["Economic work earns money.","Non-economic work is also valuable."],
 ["m|Teaching is an|economic activity|non-economic activity|play|Pay.","t|Cooking for family is non-economic.|T|Yes.","m|Helping neighbours is|non-economic|economic|illegal|Free.","t|Only paid work is important.|F|All.","m|A farmer's work is|economic|non-economic|none|Earn.","s|Work for money is called ___ activity. One word.|economic|Economic.","m|Community cleaning is|participation|nothing|noise|Together.","t|Work has value.|T|Yes."])
L("economic-activities-around-us","primary-secondary-and-tertiary-sectors","Primary, secondary and tertiary sectors","Raju saw wheat grow in a field, a mill make flour and a shop sell bread.\n\"All three are linked,\" said his teacher.",
 ["The primary sector takes things from nature: farming, fishing, mining. The secondary sector makes things from them: flour mills, factories. The tertiary sector gives services: teaching, banking, transport and shops.","The sectors depend on each other. Farmers supply wheat to mills, mills supply flour to bakers and shops sell bread.","A growing economy has more people in secondary and tertiary work."],
 ["primary sector","secondary sector","tertiary sector"],("Classify farming, a factory and a bank.",[("Farming takes from nature: primary.","Primary."),("A factory makes goods: secondary.","Secondary."),("A bank gives service: tertiary.","Tertiary.")]),
 ("a bank is in the primary sector.",["A bank gives a service.","That is tertiary."],["Wrong sector."]),
 ["Primary takes, secondary makes, tertiary serves.","Sectors depend on each other."],
 ["m|Farming is|primary|secondary|tertiary|Nature.","t|A factory is secondary.|T|Yes.","m|Teaching is|tertiary|primary|secondary|Service.","t|A bank is in the primary sector.|F|Tertiary.","m|Fishing is|primary|tertiary|secondary|Nature.","s|Making goods in a factory is the ___ sector. One word.|secondary|Secondary.","m|The three sectors|depend on each other|never meet|are the same|Linked.","t|Mining is primary.|T|Yes."])
